<Econometrics title="What did the number leave out?" description="An interactive investigation of measurement: one story, a worked undergraduate guide, and a doctoral companion on representations, identification, and decisions." section="measurement">
  <MeasurementLab />
  <section class="m-research-note"><div class="ea-shell"><h2>A measurement is an argument about the world.</h2><div><p>This investigation connects econometrics, psychometrics, qualitative inquiry, measurement theory, and decision theory. Each has something to say about the distance between an experience and its numerical record.</p><p>The mathematical results have established foundations. The proposed research and teaching protocol is still a proposal. Its sources, open problems, and tests that could disconfirm its educational promise belong in the same document.</p><a href="/econometrics/measurement/technical/">Read the technical companion and research agenda</a></div></div></section>
